                            <comment id="15234841" author="githubbot" created="Mon, 11 Apr 2016 10:24:13 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;GitHub user ptupitsyn opened a pull request:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/629&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/629&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-2970&quot; title=&quot;.NET: CompiledQuery fails with embedded const parameters&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-2970&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-2970&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; .NET: Fix CompiledQuery parameter validation&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    All CompiledQuery parameters must come from the enclosing func arguments.&lt;br/&gt;
    Constants are not allowed. There was a shortcut for zero and one arg compiled query that excluded the validation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can merge this pull request into a Git repository by running:&lt;/p&gt;

